+# B1 operator apparatus correction — submitted for narrow independent review
+
+Date: 2026-09-26. This records implementation and component evidence, not B1 launch fitness or a perceptual result. The exact new local checkpoint, parent, branch and worktree are in the delivered `CHECKPOINT.json`; this report is committed with that checkpoint.
+
+## Authority and preserved inputs
+
+Jason authorized two apparatus corrections: the reviewed display-side chemistry-hidden condition and the interactive prepared/paused/running/ended lifecycle. The controlling request is `832f5af3-01d7-417d-83b2-4e889158997a/Pasted text.txt`, preserved in the review package. P remains `6bc9683b54e4fa80136fe8534d7713e2a250a95f`; the parent apparatus is `68db2c581f07200966d699a4f55a65f9b96df1e9`.
+
+The complete held B1 delivery was read and its 124 payload/archive files inventoried before implementation. Held review/custody identity `45d71cd121f823368401b11c4a1010d509af3224f49168ad528653274d0e7543` remains historical and NON-LAUNCHABLE. Its bytes, initial snapshots, protocols, fixture definitions and horizons were not modified. Sealed manifests were treated as inert data; snapshots were checked as bytes, never loaded into an Engine. No sealed geometry or evaluator state is included in this report or the portable package.
+
+Orientation used `00_LOOM_CURRENT_STATE(2).md`, the current workbench instructions/map/status, the held packet, and `P_COUPLING_COMMISSIONING_DESIGN_v0_1_REVIEW_DRAFT.md`. The current workbench records A0–A5 as bounded physical evidence and B1 as held; older unexecuted-A5 statuses retain their dated meanings. The held packet's `PROTOCOL_CONTRACT.json` requires preserving an early-stop prefix without resuming. This is consistent with ordinary pause between 0.1-second decisions in the commissioning design. No conflicting lifecycle contract was found.
+
+## Defects and implemented correction
+
+`OPEN_ISSUE_B1_INTERFACE.md` identifies B1-H1: the old apparatus rejects every display intervention except `none`. B1-H2/H3 identify a page that looks paused during a hold, accepts queued submissions, supplies only an offline launcher, and can continue to look actionable after closure. The pre-correction fixture demonstrates the old chemistry rejection and that two submissions can produce twenty native steps instead of one ten-step hold. These are apparatus findings; they establish no perceptual, P or world failure.
+
+The new `operator_view.py` copies the actual sensor history and omits raw indices 10–13 from every operator row in CHEMISTRY-HIDDEN. It creates no zero, null, placeholder number, chemistry aggregate or estimated replacement. The result has 25 actual coordinates: 10 light, 8 contact and 7 proprioception. Actual E/I at its original cadence, commands and notes remain. FULL-RAW retains its schema-1, 29-coordinate payload and actual values. The new hidden schema is version 2. The condition and implementation hash are part of exact execution identity; an unimplemented label or mismatched implementation is rejected.
+
+Raw `SensorHistory`, native sensor recording, physical chemistry, snapshots and evaluator truth remain complete. Human decision records instead contain exactly the permitted display used for that decision. The validator checks both the full physical history and its declared operator projection. A manufactured paired 0.2-second check produced identical final physical state and identical native, wave, event and full sensor records in the two display modes.
+
+`HumanGateway` now attaches only to a fresh unadvanced human case. Starting changes PREPARED to PAUSED without stepping. One accepted decision consumes its token, enters RUNNING, executes the existing bounded hold, and returns to PAUSED or ENDED. The server rejects overlapping and delayed duplicate requests. The page disables controls before sending, rejects a second double-click event and key-repeat, and never automatically retries an uncertain command. Closing or refreshing a paused page does not issue a command. An ended interactive case cannot restart or resume, including after an administrative stop.
+
+The explicit future live factory checks execution authority before loading an initial state or creating a run directory. It was tested only for rejection of an ungranted manufactured manifest. No held case was launched. Operator routes expose only the page, a validated condition-specific payload and a closed lifecycle envelope; there is no evaluator/file/debug service. Error responses and startup messages are generic. Private failures remain in private receipts. See `CHEMISTRY_DEPRIVATION_INFORMATION_FLOW.md` and `LIVE_OPERATOR_STATE_MACHINE.md` for exact boundaries.
