+# Interactive sensor-only lifecycle specification
+
+The controlling held `PROTOCOL_CONTRACT.json` permits one bounded decision at a time and forbids resume/retry/replacement after an early stop. The commissioning design's pauses between decisions remain available. An ended case cannot be reopened.
+
+| Current state | Request / event | Next state | World effect |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| PREPARED | Permitted display/read/refresh | PREPARED | None |
+| PREPARED | Explicit start with current token | PAUSED | None |
+| PREPARED | Command | Rejected | None |
+| PAUSED | Display/read/refresh/reconnect/deliberate | PAUSED | None |
+| PAUSED | Valid paired command + current token | RUNNING | Exactly the existing declared hold, subject to existing stops |
+| RUNNING | Last-complete permitted display read | RUNNING | Read itself adds no steps |
+| RUNNING | Any additional command/start/end | Rejected | No second hold; current authorized hold remains bounded |
+| RUNNING | Hold completes with no stop | PAUSED | No extra step after the hold |
+| RUNNING | Case deadline / physical terminal / resource stop / apparatus failure | ENDED | Preserve prefix; no further actuation |
+| PREPARED or PAUSED | Explicit end / shutdown / detected wall limit | ENDED | Bookkeeping only; no physical step |
+| ENDED | Any command/start/resume | Rejected | None, irreversible |
+| ENDED | Permitted display/read | ENDED | None |
+
+## Physical and wall clocks
+
+The gateway never steps an Engine for polling, display, refresh, connection closure, start or end. Paused fields, body expenditure, native/neural state and simulation RNG do not advance. Five seconds and five minutes of real deliberation are tested with manufactured wall-clock objects and the complete physical-state hash. Opaque request tokens use operating-system randomness, never the simulation RNG.
+
+The existing command pair is still bounded by [-1,1] on each actuator, with an unchanged 0.1-second hold and 0.01-second native steps. Existing integer-index deadline handling and physical-clock validation remain byte-identical. No batching, repeated-until-success command, macro, pause expenditure, new controller gain or action assistance is supplied.
+
+Administrative wall time includes deliberation. Expiry while paused can write an end receipt but cannot consume simulated time. Wall expiry is checked on reads/claims; no background simulation exists. Storage and native stops keep their existing runner checks. A case that reaches a resource stop becomes ENDED even if its historical receipt label is `administrative_pause`; interactive continuation is prohibited.
+
+## Single decision and concurrency
+
+The gateway claims a current opaque revision token under a lock before entering RUNNING. That token is invalidated immediately. The bounded execution runs outside the lock so readers can obtain the copied last-complete permitted display. Publication returns the next PAUSED token only after the hold finishes. A delayed request with the consumed token is rejected even if it arrives after the case has become paused again. No queue is used.
+
+The client shows RUNNING and disables controls before sending. It ignores the second browser double-click event and suppresses held-key repeat; the server token check independently rejects duplicates. Response epochs stop stale read replies from overwriting a newer state/token. An uncertain request locks action controls and requires an explicit permitted refresh; the browser never resubmits. Refresh and reconnect use GET only.
+
+Closing a paused page sends no command and leaves the world inert. Closing/disconnecting during a hold does not create a second hold and does not promise cancellation of a command already accepted. A server shutdown joins a bounded in-flight request before ending the case. An abrupt process/OS failure is not claimed recoverable; the partial record remains evidence and continuation is not authorized.
+
+## Guard and persistence surfaces
+
+`HumanGateway` requires a fresh sensor-human run with zero advanced steps and no pending decision. It records `operator_lifecycle` in the restart session and writes lifecycle audit rows. `Run.begin_command` and `Run.advance` reject calls outside RUNNING when this lifecycle is attached. `Run.close` sets ENDED before writing final state. `Run` construction from any session carrying an interactive lifecycle is rejected, so loading a restart cannot re-enable an ended case. Existing unattached low-level manufactured pause/resume tests remain valid and are not a human continuation workflow.
+
+The UI envelope contains only schema, lifecycle, display condition, decision token, permitted sensors and offline status. It exposes no private stop cause. Private receipts retain the actual cause and errors for later evaluation. Offline review cannot actuate. The explicit live factory rejects missing authority before state load and output creation. This task neither launched that factory against held state nor generated its required B1 authority.
+
+## Required review evidence and limits
+
+Tests cover prepared guards; paused physical clock/RNG/expenditure; duplicate, overlapping and delayed submissions; HTTP/DOM behavior; refresh/reconnect; closed page connection; all stop categories; generic errors; and rejection of interactive resume. The actual browser appearance check used an invented fixed-time transport with no Engine, complemented by final automated DOM checks. These tests do not establish human competence, 30-second interactive throughput, exhaustive concurrency correctness or B1 launch fitness.
