+# B1 apparatus-only correction review
+
+Start with [the correction report](B1_OPERATOR_APPARATUS_CORRECTION_REPORT.md), then review the [information-flow map](CHEMISTRY_DEPRIVATION_INFORMATION_FLOW.md), [interactive lifecycle](LIVE_OPERATOR_STATE_MACHINE.md), and [A–L matrix](RED_GREEN_MATRIX.md).
+
+Evidence summaries committed here:
+
+- `REGRESSION_RESULTS.json`: final 204 worktree and 204 portable passes, prior regression logs, and fault/control runs.
+- `FINAL_PRESERVATION.json`: byte identities, committed-blob comparisons and unchanged held-file count. `P_CONFIG_WORLD_UNCHANGED.json` preserves the preceding byte/AST proof.
+- `STATIC_HELD_COMPATIBILITY.json`: inert compatibility only, with no private fixture contents or new authorities.
+- `RUNTIME_RECORD.json`, `SOURCE_IDENTITIES.json`, `UI_REVIEW.json`, `EXECUTION_SCOPE_RECORD.json`: provenance and explicit boundaries.
+
+The portable review package additionally contains the exact checkpoint/diff, complete source/configuration/tests, existing lawful component cache, raw JUnit/log evidence, manufactured component records and the public held contracts. Its `PAYLOAD_MANIFEST.json` covers every other package file. It includes neither the sealed B1 fixture nor a new launch object. The ZIP is a review delivery, not execution authorization.
+
+All execution in this correction is component/manufactured testing. No prepared positive control, B1 or ecological run/replay was performed. Stop for independent correction review; do not infer launch fitness from this checkpoint.
