+# Consequential A–L fault/control matrix
+
+All twelve final injected faults produced the expected single assertion failure, then the unmutated control passed. None of the RED results is a collection/import error. Exact logs, JUnit outputs and source identities are in `evidence/fault-matrix-sealed` in the portable package. Production files were not mutated between fault and control; the detached/component fixture enables the named fault through `B1_FAULT`.
+
+| ID | Deliberate fault | Observable RED assertion | GREEN coverage |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| A | Reinstate old `none`-only guard | old rejection | Exact implemented hidden identity accepted; bad identity rejected; mode changes authority digest |
+| B | Supply complete chemistry-bearing payload | CHEMISTRY PAYLOAD LEAK | Every row has only the 25 permitted actual coordinates |
+| C | Bypass client schema validation to simulate CSS-only hiding | CSS-ONLY MASK EXPORTED CHEMISTRY | Invalid data withheld from DOM and download; hidden/full display checks |
+| D | Zero physical chemistry before projection | DISPLAY DEPRIVATION ALTERED PHYSICAL RAW RECORD | Projection leaves source object unchanged; separate paired actual-record equality test |
+| E | Advance time during paused read | PAUSED CLOCK/RNG/EXPENDITURE BREACH E | Complete physical state unchanged |
+| F | Draw simulation RNG during paused read | PAUSED CLOCK/RNG/EXPENDITURE BREACH F | Complete physical state unchanged |
+| G | Charge energy during paused read | PAUSED CLOCK/RNG/EXPENDITURE BREACH G | Complete physical state unchanged |
+| H | Accept a consumed token again | DUPLICATE CREATED EXTRA HOLD | One actual ten-native-step hold and one decision record |
+| I | Accept another entry while running | OVERLAPPING EXECUTIONS ACCEPTED | One entered execution; controlled synchronization stub, no physical trajectory |
+| J | Step adapter after end | ENDED ADVANCED WORLD | No physical state change; start/resume also rejected |
+| K | Step on display GET during refresh/reconnect | REFRESH/RECONNECT ADVANCED WORLD | Repeated page/session/sensor reads remain inert |
+| L | Apply omission to FULL-RAW | FULL RAW LOST CHEMISTRY | Full payload equals source exactly and retains all 29 actual values |
+
+The baseline `BEFORE_CORRECTION` evidence separately ran two expected failures against unmodified 68db source: genuine hidden rejection and duplicate extra hold. The A fault above deliberately reinstates the old guard in a component fixture; it is not presented as an independent baseline execution. Fault C's disabled validator is deliberately adversarial; actual server projection and server schema validation provide an additional earlier boundary.
+
+New components use invented/manufactured states only. Fault H/J/K execute small explicit manufactured holds/steps to make failure consequential; I uses a blocking function to detect overlapping entry without evolving a world. The paired validation test reconstructs only its manufactured record. No held B1/positive-control/ecological fixture was executed or replayed. Supporting HTTP tests probe denied evaluator/file routes, generic errors, extra metadata/aggregate rejection and delayed duplicates. Node tests check DOM, downloads, fast/delayed double clicks, key repeat and lifecycle presentation.
